---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { MotionDemo } from '../../components/MotionDemo';
import { OverlayDemo } from '../../components/OverlayDemo';
import { ModeComparison } from '../../components/ModeComparison';
---
<Layout path="/motion/">
  <div class="wrap page-intro"><p class="kicker">Quiet, responsive, purposeful</p><h1>Show what<br />changed.</h1><p class="lead">A small shift keeps your place. A quick tonal change confirms an action. Motion follows your input.</p></div>
  <div class="wrap motion-reference"><section><h2>Control transition</h2><p>Replay a 200 ms response. The final arrangement remains legible when reduced motion removes the travel.</p><MotionDemo client:load /></section><section><h2>Context into focus</h2><p>A 240 ms overlay gives a local task its own space. Escape and the close control return you to the trigger.</p><OverlayDemo client:visible /></section><section><h2>A change in context</h2><p>Tabs exchange related content without moving the surrounding page.</p><ModeComparison client:visible /></section><section><h2>Motion that keeps your place</h2><p>Use motion to confirm input, explain a relationship, or preserve context as a surface opens. Begin in response to a person’s action. Keep controls available during a transition and let a new action interrupt it; never make someone wait for decoration.</p><h3>Timing, easing, distance</h3><p>Small feedback takes 160–200 ms. Overlays take 240 ms; a larger rearrangement can take 320 ms. Reserve 520 ms for a deliberate editorial reveal. These are Subtle’s timing choices, not durations prescribed by Apple or Material.</p><p>Use <code>cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)</code> for a soft ease-out. Keep control travel to 2–8 px, contextual entrances to 8–16 px, and scale close to 1. A sheet travels only far enough to establish its edge. Avoid overshoot in working data and automatic looping.</p><h3>Reduced motion</h3><p>Honor <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>: remove translation, scaling, stagger, and smooth scrolling. Keep the final state, focus, labels, and confirmations. Chart series use a single 220 ms ease-out entrance when motion is allowed; reduced motion shows final values without interpolation, including when the preference changes.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/motion">Apple HIG: Motion</a> informs responsive feedback and accessibility. <a class="text-link" href="https://m3.material.io/styles/motion/overview/how-it-works">Material 3: Motion</a> informs continuity and transitions between related states. Subtle adapts these principles to a quieter web vocabulary.</p></section><section><h2>One motion vocabulary</h2><div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Motion token table, scroll horizontally"><table class="data-table"><caption>Subtle motion tokens</caption><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Duration</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[['Fast','160 ms','Small feedback'],['Control','200 ms','Control response'],['Overlay','240 ms','Dialog and sheet'],['Layout','320 ms','Related arrangement'],['Editorial','520 ms','A deliberate reveal']].map(([role,duration,use]) => <tr><td>{role}</td><td>{duration}</td><td>{use}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="reference-note">Reduced motion disables travel and limits animation and transition durations to 0.01 ms. Every control and state remains available.</p></section><section class="motion-sources"><h2>References to explore</h2><p>The brief points to <a class="text-link" href="https://x.com/noahelhadedy/status/2097581354837770703">@noahelhadedy’s motion resource post</a>. The reading list below follows the eight resources in that post, verified by Hermes through web search.</p><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://21st.dev/">21st.dev</a> — discovery of component ideas.</li><li><a href="https://motion-primitives.com/">Motion Primitives</a> — small transitions and composed motion.</li><li><a href="https://reactbits.dev/">React Bits</a> — interaction and layout experiments.</li><li><a href="https://www.hover.dev/">Hover.dev</a> — tactile component responses.</li><li><a href="https://ui.aceternity.com/">Aceternity UI</a> — interaction discovery.</li><li><a href="https://www.microinteractionsui.com/">MicroInteractions UI</a> — focused feedback studies.</li><li><a href="https://magicui.design/">Magic UI</a> — restrained reveal and list ideas.</li><li><a href="https://annnimate.com/">annnimate.com</a> — motion studies; the name uses three n’s.</li></ul><p>These are inspiration and research references. The examples here use owned Subtle presentation and CSS transitions; linking a library does not mean its code or animation engine is installed.</p></section></div>
</Layout>
